{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\"\n       xmlns:event=\"https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event\"\n       version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"idle\">\n  <state id=\"idle\">\n    <transition event=\"order\" target=\"done\"\n                event:schema='{\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"item\": {\"$ref\": \"item.json\"}}}'/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"done\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml092-event-schema-external-ref.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml092-event-schema-external-ref.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":93,"endLine":6,"startColumn":82,"startLine":6}}}],"message":{"markdown":"the inline schema of `<transition>` has a reference the compiler cannot keep: `item.json` at `/properties/item/$ref` names another resource\n\n**Note:** no schema is fetched: a `$ref` may only name a fragment of the same file (`#/$defs/Item`); when `event:schema` selects part of a file with a pointer, the references it uses are bundled into the result, which is impossible for schemas that rely on `$id`, `$anchor`, plain-name fragments, or dynamic references\n\n**Help:** copy the referenced schema into the same file and reference it by JSON Pointer, or reference the whole file without a fragment\n\n**Spec:** JSON Schema 2020-12 Core","text":"the inline schema of `<transition>` has a reference the compiler cannot keep: `item.json` at `/properties/item/$ref` names another resource"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":342,"start":331},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML092"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"no schema is fetched: a `$ref` may only name a fragment of the same file (`#/$defs/Item`), and one naming another resource is rejected rather than left dangling. When `event:schema` selects part of a file with a pointer, the references that part uses are bundled into the embedded schema; a part that relies on `$id`, `$anchor`, plain-name fragments, or dynamic references cannot be moved and is rejected"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: copy the referenced schema into the same file and reference it by JSON Pointer, or reference the whole file without a fragment.\n\nSpecification: JSON Schema 2020-12 Core §8.2.3.1 Direct References with $ref\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML092` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/json-schema-core#section-8.2.3.1","id":"SCXML092","name":"SCXML092","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an `event:schema` has a reference the compiler cannot keep"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}